/antlr/prelude.cljc:252:    ;; depth), so every snapshot the C1 forms take inside the body is of\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc:253:    ;; that record and resumes from any caller depth. It starts at the call\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc:254:    ;; depth of its first resumer; every way back restores the caller's\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc:255:    ;; record whole, so no depth leaks across the crossing in either\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc:287:                                              :caller-ctx (cell/get py.rt/ctx)))\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc:290:                            (do (cell/set! py.rt/ctx (get c :ctx))\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc:306:             (cell/set! py.rt/ctx (get c :caller-ctx))\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc:326:                                        :ctx (cell/get py.rt/ctx)))\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc:327:                    (cell/set! py.rt/ctx (get c :caller-ctx))\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc:1658:           (cell/set! py.rt/ctx (py/ctx nil 0 nil))\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc:1689:   ;; raised by the safepoint hook prelude's depth accounting; a builtin\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc:1766:  (-> '[[py.rt/ctx (cell/new (py/ctx nil 0 nil))]\ntest/yang/python/antlr/safepoint_test.cljc:481:(defn- depth\ntest/yang/python/antlr/safepoint_test.cljc:500:                            (fn [vm] [(vm/blocked? vm) (depth vm)])))\ntest/yang/python/antlr/safepoint_test.cljc:510:;; Recursion (slice 2): depth accounting at :call and :return\ntest/yang/python/antlr/safepoint_test.cljc:531:  (testing \"the default limit, exactly: f(999) is 1000 frames and completes;\ntest/yang/python/antlr/safepoint_test.cljc:533:            probe(1) finds the limit at 1000 frames\"\ntest/yang/python/antlr/safepoint_test.cljc:538:(defn- limited\ntest/yang/python/antlr/safepoint_test.cljc:539:  \"`A'` for `pk` run under recursion limit `n`, set before the module runs.\"\ntest/yang/python/antlr/safepoint_test.cljc:542:    #(u/then (u/sexp->uast (list 'py.sp/set-recursion-limit! n)) %)))\ntest/yang/python/antlr/safepoint_test.cljc:545:(deftest escape-restores-depth-test\ntest/yang/python/antlr/safepoint_test.cljc:546:  (testing \"under limit 100: a raise through 50 frames with finally restores\ntest/yang/python/antlr/safepoint_test.cljc:547:            the depth saved at the catching try, so probe finds 100 frames\ntest/yang/python/antlr/safepoint_test.cljc:548:            again, neither fewer (depth left high) nor more (depth left\ntest/yang/python/antlr/safepoint_test.cljc:550:            frame's depth: while a RecursionError unwinds, the finally of\ntest/yang/python/antlr/safepoint_test.cljc:551:            each of frames 1..99 calls h() within the limit; only frame\ntest/yang/python/antlr/safepoint_test.cljc:555:            (hooked (limited programs/unwind 100)))))\ntest/yang/python/antlr/safepoint_test.cljc:558:(deftest generator-depth-test\ntest/yang/python/antlr/safepoint_test.cljc:559:  (testing \"under limit 100: a generator owns its dynamic context. Started\ntest/yang/python/antlr/safepoint_test.cljc:560:            21 frames down, it keeps that depth when resumed from the top\ntest/yang/python/antlr/safepoint_test.cljc:565:            (hooked (limited programs/generators 100)))))\ntest/yang/python/antlr/safepoint_test.cljc:574:(deftest set-recursion-limit-test\ntest/yang/python/antlr/safepoint_test.cljc:575:  (testing \"a lower limit takes effect\"\ntest/yang/python/antlr/safepoint_test.cljc:577:            (hooked (limited programs/probe 50))))\ntest/yang/python/antlr/safepoint_test.cljc:578:  (testing \"the limit reads back: the default, then the one set\"\ntest/yang/python/antlr/safepoint_test.cljc:584:                            '(do (py/print (py/conj [] (py.sp/recursion-limit)))\ntest/yang/python/antlr/safepoint_test.cljc:585:                                 (py.sp/set-recursion-limit! 50)\ntest/yang/python/antlr/safepoint_test.cljc:586:                                 (py/print (py/conj [] (py.sp/recursion-limit)))))))))))\ntest/yang/python/antlr/safepoint_test.cljc:587:  (testing \"an invalid argument raises the Python error and keeps the limit\"\ntest/yang/python/antlr/safepoint_test.cljc:588:    (doseq [[arg error message] [[0 \"ValueError\" \"recursion limit must be greater or equal than 1\"]\ntest/yang/python/antlr/safepoint_test.cljc:589:                                 [-3 \"ValueError\" \"recursion limit must be greater or equal than 1\"]\ntest/yang/python/antlr/safepoint_test.cljc:598:                                    (list 'fn [] (list 'py.sp/set-recursion-limit! arg))\ntest/yang/python/antlr/safepoint_test.cljc:600:                                       (do (py/print (py/conj [] (py.sp/recursion-limit)))\n|                     |                 | on the host calls back. Needs frame  |\n|                     |                 | records and a re-entrancy flag.      |\n|                     |                 | Observation-only profilers and       |\n|                     |                 | coverage stay telemetry stream       |\n|                     |                 | observers.                           |\n+---------------------+-----------------+--------------------------------------+\n| Green threads       | `:loop`,        | A run queue of continuations in a    |\n|                     | `:call`         | cell. The hook counts safepoints and |\n|                     |                 | switches every N, capturing with the |\n|                     |                 | flag-cell pattern of `py/call-ec`.   |\n|                     |                 | All threads live in one task and one |\n|                     |                 | heap. `py/raise` itself emits the    |\n|                     |                 | `:exception` trace event.            |\n+---------------------+-----------------+--------------------------------------+\n| `RecursionError`    | `:call`,        | Entry increments and checks the      |\n|                     | `:return`       | depth; normal exit decrements it; an |\n|                     |                 | escape restores the depth saved at   |\n|                     |                 | capture.                             |\n+---------------------+-----------------+--------------------------------------+\n```\n\nDepth, handlers, and the current frame form one dynamic-context record\nin one cell, generalizing `py.rt/handlers`. An exception can unwind many\nframes, so an escape restores the whole record saved at capture, as\n`py/try` and `py/call-ec` already do for the handler stack; a thread\nswitch swaps the whole record. Without that, thread B's raise would\ninvoke thread A's handler. Hooks never test the continuation\nrepresentation, so mob D7 does not affect them.\n\nComposition and cost:\n\n- There are three switches: which stream the evaluator observes, which\n  kinds the profile maps, and whether the hook prelude is loaded. An\n  empty profile is the identity, A' = A. A derived program run without\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
